{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target the existing Spring XD distributed runtime codebase (Dirt/Admin/Container/SingleNode), using its module model (source, processor, sink, job), message bus abstraction, and module registry as the foundation for all changes.",
    "U1: Introduce a pluggable codec strategy based on Spring Integration serializers/codec interfaces, exposed through module options (e.g., --encoder/--decoder or --codec) on the Kafka source, Kafka sink, and Kafka message bus, with sensible defaults (String/byte[]) to preserve backward compatibility.",
    "U2: Implement the gpfdist sink as an XD sink module embedding a GPFDIST-protocol-compatible HTTP endpoint that formats incoming payloads into gpfdist-consumable text/CSV records, with module options for GPDB/HAWQ connection, target external table, delimiter, and format; external table DDL is assumed pre-created or configurable.",
    "U3: Build the admin UI infrastructure with AngularJS and a Node.js/Grunt-based front-end build, integrating the Flo (JointJS-based) library for stream/job graph rendering, backed by the existing admin server REST endpoints; integrate UI build into the Gradle build.",
    "U4: Realize the end-to-end Kafka use case as a reproducible demo (scripted/dockerized Kafka + ZooKeeper + XD topology, e.g., high-volume http|kafka style streams), including a load-generation harness and throughput/latency measurement scripts.",
    "U5: Adopt the tasklet approach for efficient file ingestion: stream file content in chunks (buffered/streaming I/O, bounded memory) inside a Spring Batch tasklet instead of pushing raw file content line-by-line over the message bus; the spike result confirms this decision.",
    "U6: Implement the gpload tasklet as a Spring Batch tasklet (usable as an XD job module) that generates a gpload YAML control file from module options, executes the gpload CLI as an external process, captures exit codes/logs, and maps failures to batch exit statuses.",
    "U7: Remove Hadoop libraries from the XD root classpath by relocating them to the HDFS module/registry classloading scope and loading them only when HDFS-based module registry or HDFS modules are in use.",
    "U8: Implement dynamic module classpaths by extending the module classloading layer (ModuleClassLoader/module options metadata) to support explicit --classpath locations and property-placeholder-driven path patterns (e.g., /lib/*.jar:/lib/${distro}/*.jar), resolved at module deployment time with appropriate parent/module classloader isolation.",
    "Testing strategy: each story includes unit tests plus integration tests (embedded Kafka/ZooKeeper for Kafka stories; a GPDB/HAWQ instance for gpfdist/gpload stories); UI covered by front-end unit tests and build verification.",
    "Documentation limited to module reference docs/README updates and demo runbooks, produced by the developer."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single senior developer (the estimator) performs all work; estimates are pure development effort in workdays (8 hours each), excluding calendar overhead, meetings, and time off.",
    "The general Spring Framework description in the specification is context only; the actual work targets the existing Spring XD codebase and its build/CI infrastructure (Gradle-based), which is already set up and accessible.",
    "Test infrastructure is available at no additional provisioning cost: a GPDB/HAWQ instance (VM or container) with gpfdist/gpload utilities for U2/U6, and an Apache Kafka + ZooKeeper ensemble for U1/U4.",
    "Flo and related front-end libraries are available as open-source dependencies; no bespoke UX/graphic design work is required beyond wiring and basic styling.",
    "Backward compatibility must be preserved: default behavior of Kafka modules, classpath, and module loading remains unchanged unless new options are explicitly used.",
    "Scope is limited to the eight user stories; production hardening, performance certification, and operations runbooks (beyond the U4 demo scripts) are out of scope.",
    "Unit and integration testing effort is included within each activity; there is no separate QA team effort.",
    "Defect fixing for issues discovered during the final integration pass is covered by the dedicated integration activity, not by the per-story activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "1.1",
      "activity_name": "Increment requirements analysis and architecture",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the eight user stories, confirm cross-cutting design (codec strategy, module classloading changes), and produce a lightweight technical design covering impacts across source/sink/bus, jobs, UI, and classpath layers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Codec strategy design",
      "activity_description": "Design the pluggable encoder/decoder abstraction and module option surface for Kafka source, sink, and bus, ensuring backward-compatible defaults.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Codec support for Kafka source and sink",
      "activity_description": "Implement configurable encoders/decoders in the Kafka source and sink modules, wiring codec selection through module options.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Codec support for Kafka message bus",
      "activity_description": "Implement configurable codec handling in the Kafka message bus binder so bus payloads can use the selected strategy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Unit and integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for codec resolution and integration tests with embedded Kafka/ZooKeeper covering custom and default codecs across source, sink, and bus.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.5",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new codec options for Kafka source, sink, and bus in the reference docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.1",
      "activity_name": "U2 - gpfdist sink design",
      "activity_description": "Design the gpfdist sink module: GPFDIST protocol handling, data formatting, module options (host, port, database, table, delimiter, format), and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - gpfdist protocol implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the sink's embedded GPFDIST-compatible HTTP endpoint and payload-to-record formatting for GPDB/HAWQ external tables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Module packaging and options metadata",
      "activity_description": "Package the module, define its options metadata/profile, and register it as an out-of-the-box sink.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.4",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Integration tests with GPDB/HAWQ",
      "activity_description": "Create integration tests and manual verification scripts that stream data through the sink into GPDB/HAWQ external tables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the gpfdist sink module options and usage examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.1",
      "activity_name": "U3 - UI project scaffolding",
      "activity_description": "Set up the admin UI front-end project (AngularJS, Node/Grunt build, dependency management) and integrate the front-end build into the Gradle build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.2",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Flo integration",
      "activity_description": "Integrate the Flo library for stream/job graph visualization, including component setup and rendering of definitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - admin_ui wiring with backend",
      "activity_description": "Wire UI views, routing, and services to the admin server REST endpoints and embed Flo views in the admin UI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - UI tests and build verification",
      "activity_description": "Add front-end unit tests and verify the combined build pipeline produces a working admin UI artifact.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.1",
      "activity_name": "U4 - E2E Kafka use-case design",
      "activity_description": "Define the demo topology, scale/performance objectives, and environment layout (Kafka, ZooKeeper, XD nodes).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.2",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Demo implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the demo: provisioning/setup scripts, stream definitions, configuration, and a load-generation harness.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.3",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Scale and performance verification",
      "activity_description": "Run throughput/latency scenarios, tune configuration, and record results demonstrating scale and performance.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Demo documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write a runbook describing how to reproduce the end-to-end Kafka use case and interpret results.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.1",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Approach analysis (spike)",
      "activity_description": "Compare tasklet-based file ingestion versus message-bus streaming; confirm the tasklet approach and define the chunked-reading design.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.2",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Streaming file-read tasklet implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement a memory-bounded, chunked/streaming file-reading tasklet usable in XD jobs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.3",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Benchmarks and tests",
      "activity_description": "Add unit/integration tests and benchmark memory/throughput against the previous line-by-line in-memory approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.1",
      "activity_name": "U6 - gpload tasklet design",
      "activity_description": "Design the gpload tasklet: control-file (YAML) generation from options, process execution model, and error mapping.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.2",
      "activity_name": "U6 - gpload tasklet implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the tasklet executing the gpload CLI as an external process with log capture, exit-code handling, and batch status integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.3",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Integration tests with GPDB",
      "activity_description": "Verify end-to-end ingestion into GPDB via gpload from representative sources, including failure-path handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.4",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the gpload tasklet/job module options and usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.1",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Hadoop dependency analysis",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the dependency graph and classloading usage of Hadoop libraries across runtime and modules; define the isolation approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.2",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Root classpath refactoring",
      "activity_description": "Refactor build and runtime classloading to remove Hadoop libraries from the root classpath and load them only for HDFS-related scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8.3",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Regression-test startup and module deployment in HDFS and non-HDFS configurations to confirm no classloading regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.1",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Dynamic module classpath design",
      "activity_description": "Design the module classpath resolution mechanism supporting explicit --classpath locations and placeholder-driven patterns (e.g., ${distro}, ${provider}).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.2",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Classloader and path-expansion implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the dynamic classloading support: option-based path expansion, wildcard resolution, and classloader isolation in the module deployment layer.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.3",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Integration tests across module types",
      "activity_description": "Test dynamic classpaths with representative cases (hdfs --distro, jpa --provider, custom module --classpath) verifying correct dependency loading.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9.4",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the dynamic classpath options and placeholder mechanism for module authors and users.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "10.1",
      "activity_name": "Overall integration testing and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run an end-to-end integration pass across all delivered stories in a distributed XD topology and fix defects discovered.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "10.2",
      "activity_name": "Build/CI updates and release packaging",
      "activity_description": "Update build scripts and CI jobs for new modules/UI artifacts and produce the packaged software increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 75
  }
}

